{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[G]When Jesse James was a lad he’d [C]killed many a [G]man,
He robbed the Glendale [D7]train,
[G]And the people they did say for [C]many miles [G]away
[G]It was robbed by [D7]Frank and Jesse [G]James.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
Poor [C]Jesse had a wife who [G]mourned for his life,
Three children - they were brave and [D7]true
But [G]that dirty little coward who [C]shot Mister [G]Howard
Has [G]laid poor Jesse [D7]in his [G]grave
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
